+Method: `editions/monroe-1.3/tools/formula_metrics.py`, as identified in the supplied results. The tool strips Markdown H1 headings and marked scene breaks, removes emphasis markers, excludes fenced notices from prose sentence/readability calculations, and treats each non-empty manuscript line as a written paragraph. It splits sentences with its documented punctuation/capital regex after protecting common abbreviations and ellipses. Syllables use a vowel-group heuristic with silent-*e* and *-le* adjustments; proper names and system terms receive the same estimate as ordinary words and can bias Flesch results.
